    "coverage_is_binding": "465 of 511 CPU-Heavy rows in SWE277 are served by public:bin, i.e. their command has no local history in that repository at prediction time. Deep local nodes are near-perfect but rare, which reproduces the leave-one-out ceiling result through runtime provenance.",
    "rss_failure": "RSS repo:exact_clause holds zero Heavy observations in both orientations, and public:bin sits near the 1% base rate, so no node reaches theta on SWE100 and the only firing band on SWE277 yields 1 TP against 84 FP. RSS-Heavy clauses do not recur as the same command within a repository in causal order, consistent with their 28 s median latency. Third independent line of evidence for RSS NO-GO, after the near-zero representation ceiling and the zero-true-positive cascade."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Development-exposed on both SWE corpora; cannot support a confirmation claim.",
    "The outcome was predicted in writing from exposed operating curves before being computed, so the gate confirms an expectation rather than testing a hypothesis.",
    "Whole-clause labels only. No future-after-t target; that needs the bounded resource timeline requested against clause_bridge.py, which is not retained.",
    "The bootstrap covers the candidate-vs-current margin at the repository cluster level; it does not correct for corpus exposure.",
    "Utility magnitudes are large mainly because current fires almost never (Disk SWE100 current TP=1 of 99), not because candidate precision is high."
  ]
